cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "nano-lm: an auditable GPT-Neo forward pass in dependency-free TypeScript"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-22
authors:
  - family-names: Shen
    given-names: Shangyan
    email: shenshangyan2001@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A hand-written implementation of the GPT-Neo transformer forward pass in
  plain TypeScript with zero runtime dependencies, bundled with the
  TinyStories-1M checkpoint (7.5 MB, fp16 safetensors). It exposes every
  intermediate of the computation — token and position embeddings, the
  residual stream after each block, per-layer per-head attention weights and
  next-token logits — and is verified token-exact against the reference
  Hugging Face implementation (greedy continuation) with logits and attention
  maps reproduced within fp16 tolerance. Includes cosine nearest-neighbour
  search over the embedding table, automatic discovery of interpretable
  attention heads (previous-token, first-token anchor, most diffuse), and
  top-k / temperature sampling utilities. Extracted from the interactive essay
  "Inside the Machine", where it powers the in-browser dissection widgets.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - transformers
  - GPT-Neo
  - interpretability
  - TypeScript
  - in-browser inference
  - machine learning education
license: MIT
